# The Fast tier's map (ADR 0073 d1, p43-2): which test files a changed path reaches. tests/lib/fast-tier.py reads it
# (its docstring holds the reach rules); `bash tests/run.sh --fast` (`make test-fast`) runs what it selects, and every
# run checks it (`fast-tier.py check`).
#
# A line is `<pattern> [FULL | NONE | HUB <entry>... | ALSO <entry>... | <entry>...]`; `#` starts a comment.
#   - A bare pattern places the path and leaves the result to its reach.
#   - An entry is a collected test path, a glob over collected tests, or @merge-task-self-tests.
#   - Every line that matches a path counts. A matching line that is not ALSO places the path; any FULL is the full
#     suite. Otherwise the result is the union of the plain entries and the reach; ALSO entries are added on top and
#     never count as reach. A path placed only by NONE lines selects only the ALSO entries of its lines (the walkers).
#   - A HUB line declares a hub: an exact path, its suites listed on it (several lines add up). A path that reaches it
#     adds its suites and the reach ends there; check (i) keeps the list whole.
#   - The same pattern may repeat on several lines.
# Patterns are repo-relative and matched segment by segment, fnmatchcase on each segment, so `*`, `?` and `[...]`
# never cross a `/`; a whole `**` segment matches zero or more segments.
# `FOREIGN <basename>...` declares names the scripts read in other roots. `FOREIGN-ONLY <name> <test>...` declares tests
# that hold the FOREIGN name <name> only as another root's file and never read this repo's, so a change to the real one
# does not select them; each line's trailing comment says what they hold it as. `OWN-LISTINGS <test>...` excuses tests
# from check (f) on one of the two kinds the selector's docstring defines; each line's trailing comment says which kind
# applies and what it lists.

FOREIGN SKILL.md CONTEXT.md README.md THREAD.md CLAUDE.md

# ---- FOREIGN-ONLY: tests that never read this repo's copy of the name (a reader stays off: repo-threads reads the real
# CONTEXT.md, fast-tier-wiring the real CLAUDE.md, inert-paths proves globs on this tree) ----
